## Critical Pitfalls — Do Not Repeat

### Signing order (Sparkle nested bundles)
Re-sign in this exact order or notarization fails with "Sparkle XPC components not signed":
1. XPC binaries (Installer, Downloader, Autoupdate, Updater)
2. XPC bundles (.xpc, Updater.app)
3. Sparkle.framework
4. Outer .app

Already implemented in `scripts/release.sh` — do not modify signing order.

### SIGPIPE with codesign + head
Never pipe `codesign --verify --deep --strict` output through `head`. SIGPIPE → exit 141 → `set -euo pipefail` kills the build. Use: `codesign --verify --deep --strict "${APP_PATH}" && echo "✓"`.

### Localizable.strings encoding
Never use `cat >>` to append to `.strings` files — corrupts encoding. Use Edit tool or direct write. If corrupted: `git checkout HEAD -- path/to/Localizable.strings`.

### Hotkey modifier matching
Only `.command`, `.shift`, `.option`, `.control` — do not compare against raw `deviceIndependentFlagsMask` (includes Caps Lock and Function → false matches).

### TCC permissions + unsigned builds
macOS TCC resets on each new unsigned build (Designated Requirement changes). Developer ID signing = stable identity = no resets. All production builds must be signed.

### `get-task-allow` blocks notarization
`com.apple.security.get-task-allow=true` → Apple rejects. Must be explicitly `false` in entitlements + re-sign with `codesign --force --entitlements` after `xcodebuild`.

### XcodeGen SPM syntax
Use `from: 2.0.0`, not `majorVersion: 2` — XcodeGen doesn't understand the latter.

