## Coding Conventions

- Karpathy principles: surgical changes, no speculative features, no overengineering
- Minimal diff — only touch what the task requires
- New LLM provider: implement protocol → register in `allProviders` → add to Help strings (EN+DE) → add to `project.yml` if new file → `make generate`
- New built-in prompt: add to `DemoPrompt.builtIn` static array in `DemoPrompt.swift`
- For every user-visible feature, provider, prompt, setting, release-flow change, or behavior change, update documentation in the same task:
  - `README.md`
  - in-app Help strings (`Tippi/Resources/en.lproj/Localizable.strings` + `de.lproj/Localizable.strings`)
  - `CHANGELOG.md`
  - project version numbers (`project.yml` `MARKETING_VERSION`, and any matching public docs)
  - Vault (`~/MWs2ndBrain/02 Projekte/Tippi.md`) when available/relevant
- Before finishing, explicitly check whether README, in-app Help, CHANGELOG, localization, and version numbers need updates. Do not leave them for later.
- `CHANGELOG.md` is the single source of truth for version history
- `README.md` is the single source of truth for feature lists and provider counts
- `release.env` is gitignored — never commit it
